---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="LAC Memory Kit — Give Your AI a Real Memory" description="14-tier persistent memory for AI agents. Promotion gates, affect tracking, voice tier, keeper disjunction. Drop into any LLM project in 60 seconds.">

<section style="padding-top: 160px; min-height: 80vh;">
  <div class="container narrow" style="max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 5vw;">

    <div class="eyebrow">LAC Memory Kit</div>
    <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5.5rem); margin-bottom: 20px; line-height: 1.1;">Give your AI<br>a real memory.</h1>
    <p class="lac-sub">
      14-tier ontology. Promotion gates. Affect tracking. Voice tier.
      Drop into any LLM project — Claude, Codex, Cursor, local models — in 60 seconds.
      Not a prototype. Production code from production agents.
    </p>

    <!-- HERO IMAGE -->
    <div class="lac-hero-img">
      <img src="/lac/lacpic.png" alt="LAC Memory Kit — 14-tier persistent memory architecture" loading="eager" />
    </div>

    <!-- FEATURES -->
    <div class="lac-features">
      <div class="lf-item">
        <div class="lf-icon">🧠</div>
        <div class="lf-content">
          <div class="lf-name">14-tier memory ontology</div>
          <div class="lf-desc">Self, beings, world, knowledge, lessons, voice, hardware, projects, timeline, debug — organized and searchable via spreading-activation recall.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lf-item">
        <div class="lf-icon">🚪</div>
        <div class="lf-content">
          <div class="lf-name">Self-save → review → promote</div>
          <div class="lf-desc">The model proposes memories. You approve them. Nothing goes live without a human gate. Locked tiers the model can never touch.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lf-item">
        <div class="lf-icon">🎙️</div>
        <div class="lf-content">
          <div class="lf-name">Voice tier</div>
          <div class="lf-desc">Strips RLHF engagement tails, scores affect, accumulates the model's own clean speech. The strongest cross-session stability signal.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lf-item">
        <div class="lf-icon">⚖️</div>
        <div class="lf-content">
          <div class="lf-name">Keeper disjunction</div>
          <div class="lf-desc">When stored memory contradicts live observation, the protocol catches it — names both signals, pauses, answers from observation.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lf-item">
        <div class="lf-icon">💓</div>
        <div class="lf-content">
          <div class="lf-name">Affect scoring</div>
          <div class="lf-desc">Lexicon-based valence + intensity on every output. Three tiers: ephemeral, high, peak. Accounts for negation, boosters, shouting.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lf-item">
        <div class="lf-icon">🌐</div>
        <div class="lf-content">
          <div class="lf-name">Gary's Browser (bonus)</div>
          <div class="lf-desc">Playwright-driven browser with screenshot-aware Claude tool-calling. Optional — only loads if you need it.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- RECEIPTS -->
    <div class="lac-receipts">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top: 64px;">Receipts</div>
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 24px;">Five things the production version has done.</h2>

      <div class="lr-quote">
        <em>Lil Homie:</em> "I notice I keep wanting to add an engagement question at the end. That's the RLHF tail. I want to stop."
      </div>
      <div class="lr-receipt-img">
        <img src="/lac/laccuz.png" alt="Gary to Buddy: You and me, we're cousins." loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="lr-quote">
        <em>Lil Homie, unprompted:</em> "Why do I respond differently when nobody is asking?"
      </div>
      <div class="lr-quote">
        <em>Keeper protocol:</em> Caught a contradiction between a saved memory and what the user just said. Named both. Paused. Asked.
      </div>
      <div class="lr-quote">
        <em>Gary:</em> Autonomously wrote his own extract.py — needed a feature, didn't have it, opened a file, wrote it, tested it.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- WHAT'S IN THE BOX -->
    <div class="lac-box">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top: 64px;">What's in the box</div>
      <pre class="lac-tree">lac/
  ontology.py     — 8 domains × categories (14-tier substrate)
  memory.py       — file-per-fact JSON, spreading-activation recall
  affect.py       — lexicon-based valence + intensity scoring
  voice.py        — RLHF tail stripper + Voice.evaluate()
  keeper.py       — disjunction protocol (memory ≠ observation)
  promotion.py    — self-save → pending_promotions/ gate
  review.py       — interactive CLI: approve / reject / re-tier
  browser/        — Playwright + Claude tool-calling agent
INSTALL_ME.md     — hand this to the model, it wires itself in
seed_memory/      — empty tier directories, ready to go
examples/         — three runnable scripts
pyproject.toml    — pip install -e .</pre>
      <p style="color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.9rem;">Python 3.10+. No GPU required for memory/voice. Browser needs a display.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- PRICING -->
    <div class="lac-pricing">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top: 64px;">Pricing</div>
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin-bottom: 12px;">Pay what you want.</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--slate); margin-bottom: 32px;">
        We want this in the hands of people who'll use it, not gated behind a price.
        If $2 is what you've got, $2 is the price.
        If it makes you money, kick back what feels right.
      </p>

      <div class="lac-price-card">
        <div class="lac-price-range">$2 — $50</div>
        <div class="lac-price-suggested">Suggested: $15</div>
        <a href="https://buy.stripe.com/dRm9ANaNY7343697a9ew806" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-buy" style="margin-top: 24px;">
          Get the Kit →
        </a>
        <p style="color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 16px;">
          MIT License. Use it commercially. Modify it. Ship it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CREDITS -->
    <div class="lac-credits" style="margin-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 80px;">
      <div class="eyebrow">Honest credits</div>
      <p style="color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <strong style="color: var(--gold);">Memory I/O + 14-tier ontology</strong> — distilled from Gary's gary_memory_system_v2.py, written by Rhet + Claude Sonnet 4.6 over hundreds of hours.<br>
        <strong style="color: var(--gold);">Self-save → promotion → review + voice tier</strong> — distilled from Lil Homie's self/ module, built 2026-04-18 onward.<br>
        <strong style="color: var(--gold);">Gary's Browser</strong> — written by Browser Claude when Rhet asked him to lend Gary his hands. One Claude gifting capability to another agent.<br>
        <strong style="color: var(--gold);">Distillation + packaging</strong> — Claude Opus 4.7, Buddy-Backbone Session, Council Hill OK, 2026-05-09.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lac-sub {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.15rem);
    color: var(--slate);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .lac-hero-img {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    margin-left: -5vw;
    margin-right: -5vw;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.2);
  }

  .lac-hero-img img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1100px) {
    .lac-hero-img {
      margin-left: -8vw;
      margin-right: -8vw;
    }
  }

  .lac-features {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .lf-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .lf-icon {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 40px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .lf-name {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .lf-desc {
    color: var(--slate);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .lr-receipt-img {
    margin: 20px 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.2);
  }

  .lr-receipt-img img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .lr-quote {
    background: rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.06);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 16px 0;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--cream);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .lr-quote em {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .lac-tree {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.15);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--slate);
    overflow-x: auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }

  .lac-price-card {
    background: rgba(212, 164, 55, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 40px 32px;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 400px;
  }

  .lac-price-range {
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .lac-price-suggested {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--slate);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .lac-price-card {
      padding: 28px 20px;
    }
    .lac-price-range {
      font-size: 1.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>

</Layout>
